course: dictionary
lesson: 2291
title: Words that name a person
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word ending in -er often names a person who does something. A cricketer is a person who plays cricket, a bat-and-ball game played by two teams of eleven. Cricket is the game, and the cricketer is the player.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «In 2018 in Cape Town, Australian cricketers were caught changing the ball with sandpaper.» The word cricketers names the people in the sentence, and the rest of the sentence tells you they were playing the game, not doing something else.
explain: Cricketers have different jobs in a team. Some are batters, who hit the ball. Some are bowlers, who throw the ball to the batter. Fielders stop the ball, and wicketkeepers guard the wicket. An all-rounder is good at both batting and bowling.
fact: A cricketer is a person who plays cricket.
fact: Cricket is a bat-and-ball game played by two teams of eleven.
fact: Cricket is very popular in the UK, Australia, New Zealand, India, Pakistan, the West Indies and South Africa, and it is played in Ireland and Canada too.
fact: Cricketers can be batters, bowlers, fielders or wicketkeepers.
fact: An all-rounder is a cricketer who is good at both batting and bowling.
fact: Phrases you may meet: «a professional cricketer» (someone paid to play) and «a young cricketer».
exercise: What is a cricketer? | A person who swims in the sea | A person who kicks a ball into a net | A person who sings in a choir | *A person who plays cricket, a bat-and-ball game for two teams of eleven
exercise: An all-rounder is good at which two things? | *Batting and bowling | Running and jumping | Swimming and diving | Fielding and wicketkeeping only
exercise: «In 2018 in Cape Town, Australian cricketers were caught changing the ball with sandpaper.» What does caught mean in this sentence? | Given a medal for winning | *Found doing something wrong | Caught a ball in a fielder's hands | Tired and sleepy
test: The ending -er often shows a person who does a job. What does -er mean in cricketer? | *A person who does the thing | A question | A very small thing | Two of something | The past of the word
test: Which of these is NOT a cricket role? | Batter | Fielder | *Goalkeeper | Bowler
exam: Mia says a cricketer is a person who plays football. What is the correct meaning? | *A person who plays cricket, a bat-and-ball game for two teams of eleven | A person who sings in a choir | A person who swims in the sea | A person who kicks a ball into a net
